# Resource usage of local execution
#
# HOST_CPUS and HOST_RAM come from the JVM of the Bazel server, which honours cgroup limits, so they
# match the developer machine.  Do not pin -XX:ActiveProcessorCount: HOST_CPUS would take that
# value on every host (CMK-39409).

# Keep a developer machine responsive while building: leave two CPUs to the desktop.
# Most actions declare one CPU, so this effectively limits how many run in parallel.
# The keyword scales with the host, so there is no fixed --jobs.
common --local_resources=cpu=HOST_CPUS-2

# Memory and persistent workers stay at Bazel's defaults (memory=HOST_RAM*.67,
# 4 workers per mnemonic): the memory check only uses each action's declared,
# estimated RAM, and more workers would only add resident memory.
